# See doc at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/master/prdoc/schema_user.json

title: "[pallet-xcm] Fix dry-run side-effects leaking into xcm-emulator process_messages()"

doc:
  - audience: [Runtime Dev]
    description: |
      `dry_run_call` and `dry_run_xcm` in `pallet-xcm` now execute inside a storage
      transaction that is always rolled back. Previously the XCM execution performed
      during a dry-run (including `Router::clear_messages()` and any XCMP queue writes)
      was committed to the underlying externalities. In xcm-emulator tests this caused
      `execute_with()` to forward the dry-run's outbound messages through
      `process_messages()`, silently mutating destination-chain state.

      The workarounds in `emulated-integration-tests-common` (`reset_ext()` calls and
      a no-op `execute_with(|| {})`) that papered over this issue have been removed.

crates:
  - name: pallet-xcm
    bump: patch
  - name: emulated-integration-tests-common
    bump: patch
